<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Fivetran NetSuite SDK Integration role.

  Purpose: a dedicated, least-privilege role for the NetSuite Connector SDK connector in this
  repo, built from scratch rather than cloned from a standard role, because:
    - "Data Warehouse Integrator" (DWI) cannot be customized/cloned (Oracle-documented
      restriction - it's tied to the licensed NetSuite Analytics Warehouse / SuiteAnalytics
      Connect subscription), and
    - "Accountant (Reviewer)" (the best customizable standard-role candidate) is missing many
      genuine transaction types present in DWI, plus the Subsidiaries (Lists) and Manage
      Accounting Periods (Setup) permissions needed for the `subsidiary`/`accountingperiod`
      tables.

  Transactions coverage strategy (revised - second pass): DWI's Transactions category has 117
  entries (read directly from a live export of that role). This file includes the 48 that
  correspond to a genuine, distinct `type` value in the transaction/transactionline/
  transactionaccountingline tables, at View. The other 69 are excluded, grouped by why:

    - 13 are "<Something> Approval" - workflow/routing on an already-created record, not a
      distinct type: Blanket Purchase Order Approval, Employee Commission Transaction Approval,
      Invoice Approval, Journal Approval, Partner Commission Transaction Approval, Purchase
      Contract Approval, Requisition Approval, Return Auth. Approval, Sales Order Approval,
      Transfer Order Approval, Vendor Bill Approval, Vendor Payment Approval, Vendor Return
      Auth. Approval.
    - Audit/security/payment-gateway features, not transaction data: Access Payment Audit Log,
      Audit Trail, Cardholder Authentication, Cardholder Authentication Event, View Payment
      Events, View Payment Result Previews.
    - Banking feed / reconciliation, unrelated to the transaction table: Personal Banking
      Information, Import Online Banking File, Matching Rules for Online Banking, Reconcile,
      Automated Cash Application.
    - Forecast/budget/quota - a different feature area entirely: Edit Forecast, Edit Manager
      Forecast, Establish Quotas, Set Up Budgets, Copy Budgets.
    - Commission module (SuiteCommissions, not core GL/AP/AR): Employee Commission Transaction,
      Partner Commission Transaction.
    - Document generation / UI utilities, not a posted record: Generate Price Lists, Generate
      Statements, Find Transaction (confirmed elsewhere to be a search-UI feature, not a
      row-visibility gate), Edit Profile, Calculate Time, Timer.
    - Staging/worksheet tools, not themselves posted transactions: Adjust Inventory Worksheet,
      Bin Putaway Worksheet, Create Allocation Schedules.
    - Admin overrides / field-level permissions, not a transaction type: Override Estimated
      Cost on Transactions, Override Payment Hold, Post Vendor Bill Variances, Posting Period
      on Transactions, Charge Rule.
    - Redundant actions on an already-covered type (the kept base-type permission already
      grants row visibility for that type): Bill Purchase Orders, Build Work Orders, Close Work
      Orders, Create Inventory Counts, Credit Returns, Deposit Application, Distribute
      Inventory, Enter Completions, Enter Opening Balances, Fulfill Orders, Fulfillment
      Request, Invoice Sales Orders, Issue Components, Mark Work Orders Built/Firmed/Released,
      Receive Order, Receive Returns, Refund Returns, Work Order Close, Work Order Completion,
      Work Order Issue.

  This classification (which of the 117 map to a genuine distinct `type` value vs. which are
  actions/utilities/reports) is domain-knowledge judgment, not verified against an authoritative
  NetSuite document that explicitly enumerates transaction type permissions vs. action
  permissions - treat it as a well-reasoned draft, not a certainty.

  Permission IDs (permkey) were verified against Oracle's official "Permission Names and IDs"
  reference (NetSuite Help Center - chapter_N3236764.html) rather than guessed from the
  permission's display name in the role UI. One disambiguation worth calling out: the UI shows
  "Quote" under Transactions, but the reference table lists the same underlying permission
  under the name "Estimate" (permkey TRAN_ESTIMATE) - confirmed to be the same permission, not
  a second/different one.

  KNOWN GAP: two of DWI's 117 Transactions entries have no corresponding row in the Permission
  Names and IDs reference table at all (not a lookup miss - confirmed absent by two separate,
  differently-worded searches), so no permkey is available for them: "Charge - Run Rules" and
  "View Gateway Asynchronous Notifications". Both would likely have been excluded under this
  file's criteria anyway (a scheduling utility and a payment-gateway notification log,
  respectively), so this is a low-priority gap, but is noted for completeness.

  None of the permkeys below have been cross-checked against the live account's own
  `rolepermissions` SuiteQL table (that query was attempted during development but failed - the
  credentials available did not have visibility into that table). The recommended way to get
  ground-truth confirmation is `suitecloud object:import -type role -scriptid
  data_warehouse_integrator` against a sandbox, which pulls DWI's real XML with
  guaranteed-correct permkeys to diff against this file.

  Two permissions worth flagging explicitly since they're easy to confuse with a similarly
  named one:
    - ADMI_LOGIN_OAUTH is classic Token-Based Authentication ("Log in using Access Tokens" -
      OAuth 1.0a, what this connector uses). It is NOT ADMI_LOGIN_OAUTH2 ("Log in using
      OAuth 2.0 Access Tokens"), which this role intentionally does not include.

  Everything outside Transactions/the three base permissions is deliberately narrow: no
  Employees, Items, Customers/Vendors-as-Lists-records, Custom Records, Reports other than
  SuiteAnalytics Workbook, or SuiteAnalytics Connect itself.
-->
<role scriptid="customrole_fivetran_netsuite_sdk">
  <name>Fivetran NetSuite SDK Integration</name>
  <centertype>ACCOUNTCENTER</centertype>
  <issalesrole>F</issalesrole>
  <issupportrole>F</issupportrole>
  <iswebserviceonlyrole>T</iswebserviceonlyrole>
  <employeerestriction>NONE</employeerestriction>
  <employeeviewingallowed>F</employeeviewingallowed>
  <restricttimeandexpenses>F</restricttimeandexpenses>
  <restrictip>F</restrictip>
  <restrictbydevice>F</restrictbydevice>
  <coreadminpermission>F</coreadminpermission>
  <permissions>

    <!-- ==================== Setup: base access required for any SuiteQL/REST call ==================== -->

    <!-- "Log in using Access Tokens" - classic TBA (OAuth 1.0a). NOT ADMI_LOGIN_OAUTH2 (OAuth 2.0). -->
    <permission><permkey>ADMI_LOGIN_OAUTH</permkey><permlevel>FULL</permlevel></permission>
    <!-- "REST Web Services" - required for SuiteTalk REST / the SuiteQL endpoint. -->
    <permission><permkey>ADMI_RESTWEBSERVICES</permkey><permlevel>FULL</permlevel></permission>
    <!-- "Manage Accounting Periods" - required for the `accountingperiod` table. -->
    <permission><permkey>ADMI_ACCTPERIODS</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>

    <!-- ==================== Reports: required for SuiteQL execution itself ==================== -->

    <!-- "SuiteAnalytics Workbook" - despite the name, this gates whether SuiteQL can execute at
         all (confirmed empirically: without it, even `SELECT 1 FROM dual` fails). It is
         unrelated to the paid SuiteAnalytics Connect add-on. Set to EDIT to match the level
         confirmed working in this build; DWI itself only carries VIEW, but that was never
         confirmed sufficient for the REST/SuiteQL path specifically (DWI uses Connect/ODBC). -->
    <permission><permkey>REPO_ANALYTICS</permkey><permlevel>EDIT</permlevel></permission>

    <!-- ==================== Lists: for the `account` and `subsidiary` tables ==================== -->

    <permission><permkey>LIST_ACCOUNT</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>
    <permission><permkey>LIST_SUBSIDIARY</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>
    <!-- "Paychecks" - Lists-category companion to TRAN_PAYCHECK below; less certain this is
         actually needed (may just be a register/list-viewing permission), included since an
         unused permission costs nothing. -->
    <permission><permkey>LIST_PAYCHECK</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>

    <!-- ==================== Transactions: genuine distinct transaction types only ====================
         48 permissions. See header comment for the full exclusion rationale (69 excluded:
         13 approvals + 56 audit/banking/forecast/commission/utility/worksheet/admin/redundant
         permissions that don't gate a distinct `type` value). -->

    <permission><permkey>TRAN_INVADJST</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Adjust Inventory -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_VENDBILL</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Bills / Vendor Bill -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_BINTRNFR</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Bin Transfer -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_BLANKORD</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Blanket Purchase Order -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_BUILD</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>           <!-- Build Assemblies -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_CASHSALE</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Cash Sale -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_CASHRFND</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Cash Sale Refund -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_CHARGE</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>          <!-- Charge (SuiteBilling) -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_CHECK</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>           <!-- Check -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_INVCOUNT</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Inventory Count -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_CARDCHRG</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Credit Card Charge -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_CARDRFND</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Credit Card Refund -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_CUSTCRED</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Credit Memo -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_FXREVAL</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>         <!-- Currency Revaluation -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_CUSTDEP</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>         <!-- Customer Deposit -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_CUSTPYMT</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Customer Payment -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_CUSTRFND</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Customer Refund -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_DEPOSIT</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>         <!-- Deposit -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_VENDCRED</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Vendor Credit -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_EXPREPT</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>         <!-- Expense Report -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_FINCHRG</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>         <!-- Finance Charge -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_CUSTINVC</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Invoice -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_ITEMRCPT</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Item Receipt -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_ITEMSHIP</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Item Shipment -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_JOURNAL</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>         <!-- Journal Entry -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_OPPRTNTY</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Opportunity -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_VENDPYMT</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Bill Payment (Pay Bills) -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_TAXPYMT</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>         <!-- Sales Tax Payment (Pay Sales Tax) -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_PURCHCON</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Purchase Contract -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_PURCHORD</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Purchase Order -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_ESTIMATE</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Quote / Estimate -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_RFQ</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>             <!-- Request For Quote -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_PURCHREQ</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Requisition -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_RTNAUTH</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>         <!-- Return Authorization -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_INVREVAL</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Inventory Cost Revaluation -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_SALESORD</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Sales Order -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_CUSTCHRG</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Statement Charge -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_STPICKUP</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Store Pickup Fulfillment -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_SYSJRNL</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>         <!-- System Journal -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_TIMEBILL</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Time Bill (Track Time) -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_TRANSFER</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Fund Transfer -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_INVTRNFR</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Inventory Transfer -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_TRNFRORD</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Transfer Order -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_UNBUILD</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>         <!-- Unbuild Assemblies -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_VENDRFQ</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>         <!-- Vendor Request For Quote -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_VENDAUTH</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>        <!-- Vendor Return Authorization -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_VENDAUTHRETURN</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>  <!-- Vendor Return -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_WORKORD</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>         <!-- Work Order -->

    <!-- ==================== Added after cross-checking against real DISTINCT type values ====================
         from this account's live transaction table (ground truth, not domain-knowledge
         inference). Several of these were WRONGLY excluded in the second pass above as
         "redundant actions on an already-covered type" - they turn out to post as their own
         genuine distinct `type` value, not just a status change on an existing record. -->

    <permission><permkey>TRAN_BINWKSHT</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>          <!-- Bin Putaway Worksheet -> type 'binworksheet' -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_DEPAPPL</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>           <!-- Deposit Application -> type 'depositapplication' -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_INVWKSHT</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>          <!-- Adjust Inventory Worksheet -> type 'inventoryworksheet' -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_WOCLOSE</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>           <!-- Work Order Close -> type 'workorderclose' -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_WOCOMPL</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>           <!-- Work Order Completion -> type 'workordercompletion' -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_WOISSUE</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>           <!-- Work Order Issue -> type 'workorderissue' -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_COMMISSN</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>          <!-- Employee Commission Transaction -> type 'commission' -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_PARTNERCOMMISSN</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>   <!-- Partner Commission Transaction - added alongside TRAN_COMMISSN; which one actually produces type 'commission' in this account wasn't disambiguated -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_SALESORDFULFILL</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>   <!-- Fulfill Orders -> type 'itemfulfillment' (TRAN_ITEMSHIP above was likely the wrong mapping for this concept) -->
    <permission><permkey>TRAN_PAYCHECK</permkey><permlevel>VIEW</permlevel></permission>          <!-- Individual Paycheck -> type 'paycheck' (not in DWI's Transactions list at all - found via separate Payroll permission research) -->

  </permissions>
</role>
